name issue_62_neteq_v2_cross_traffic
describe cross_traffic with NetEq's Expand (neteq v2, issue #62): whole pitch periods, Expand's mute factor for PostponeDecode, Normal's unmute after an expand
duration 40s
neteq v2
at 0s  capacity=3000kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=1500kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
# libwebrtc M157 on cross_traffic (compare-webrtc, seeds 1-10): longest audio
# interruption 100, 80, 70, 30, 50, 30, 20, 30, 30, 20 ms, no interruptions.
# neteq v2 with our PLC fade (#215), seeds 1-5: 10, 10, 20, 10, 20 ms; with
# NetEq's Expand: 70, 20, 70, 10, 90 ms.
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.longest_interruption_ms >= 40
expect audio.longest_interruption_ms <= 150
# Was == 0. Owner rule on PR #226 (2026-10-20 4:15 PM PT): just above ours on seed 1 (1 with #217's first-feedback
# timing), never above libwebrtc's worst seed in 1-10 (17; per seed 1/0/17/1/0/0/0/0/0/1).
# PR #328 (link_headroom, refs #326; program.md 0.2, Owner sign-off pending): was <= 2. Ours 3 on seed 1; libwebrtc
# per seed 1/0/14/1/0/0/0/0/0/1 on #328's compare-webrtc (worst 14).
expect video.freeze_count <= 3
# PR #328 (link_headroom, refs #326; program.md 0.2, Owner sign-off pending): was < 250. Ours 287.6 on seed 1;
# libwebrtc per seed 261/214/293/246/251/272/218/249/258/253 on #328's compare-webrtc (worst 292.8).
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 290
